Libraries built with `-lib` are reproducible

`-lib` used to write the time it ran, and the building user's ids, into the
header of every member of the library it wrote. Building the same sources
twice gave two different libraries, so a build system that compares outputs
or caches by content saw a change where there was none.

Each member header now records a zero time, owner and group, as `llvm-ar`
writes them by default and `ar D` does. A module the compiler wrote has mode
`0644`; an object file named on the command line keeps the mode of the file.
